SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Programme presidentiel","publisher":"Presidence RDC","publication_date":"unknown","url":"https://www.presidence.cd/programme-presidentiel","claim":"The presidential program was initiated at Tshisekedi's initiative, refined by experts under his cabinet, and converted from 20 pillars to 15 pillars around a vision of building a modern state and defeating poverty.","locator":"presentation, lines 68-71","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official presidential program page directly describes the program's origin and structure.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Program framing used during the 2022 period.","ruler_attribution":"High attribution: directly presented as Tshisekedi's initiative and cabinet-supervised program design.","contrary_evidence":["Official self-presentation may overstate coherence or implementation."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Projet de loi de finances pour l'exercice 2022","publisher":"Ministère du Budget, DRC","publication_date":"September 2021","url":"https://www.budget.gouv.cd/wp-content/uploads/budget2022/projet/document_1_expose_des_motifs_et_annexes_loi_plf_2022_vs_final.pdf","claim":"The 2022 budget proposal says the government would continue free basic education, universal health coverage, population registration, election preparation, results-based budgeting, public-administration modernization, tax reform, and anti-corruption efforts.","locator":"p.2, lines 25-43","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary budget proposal states declared priorities and implementation architecture.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Immediately precedes and shapes the 2022 fiscal year.","ruler_attribution":"High attribution to the Tshisekedi government; the document itself says these are program actions.","contrary_evidence":["A proposal is not implementation; later execution must be checked separately."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Projet de loi de finances pour l'exercice 2022","publisher":"Ministère du Budget, DRC","publication_date":"September 2021","url":"https://www.budget.gouv.cd/wp-content/uploads/budget2022/projet/document_2_expose_general_plf_2022_et_annexes_vs_finale.pdf","claim":"The budget framework prioritizes social and productive investment, peace in the east, the 2023 elections, and domestic revenue gains through anti-fraud and tax reforms.","locator":"p.4, lines 121-126","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary budget framework spells out fiscal and policy priorities.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 budget framework within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"High attribution to the government program under Tshisekedi.","contrary_evidence":["Budget priorities do not by themselves prove delivery."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Projet de loi de finances pour l'exercice 2022","publisher":"Ministère du Budget, DRC","publication_date":"September 2021","url":"https://www.budget.gouv.cd/wp-content/uploads/budget2022/projet/document_1_expose_des_motifs_et_annexes_loi_plf_2022_vs_final.pdf","claim":"The proposed 2022 budget funds free primary education operating costs, school and hospital supplies, agricultural inputs, and 500 billion FC for election operations.","locator":"p.6-7 and p.34, lines 162-185 and 1064-1068","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary budget tables and narrative specify spending lines and earmarks.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 fiscal year.","ruler_attribution":"High attribution to the Tshisekedi government because this is the enacted program funding plan.","contrary_evidence":["Appropriations can exceed execution; spending outcomes need separate evidence."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Réunion d'évaluation du programme de développement à la base des 145 territoires","publisher":"Presidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-09-15","url":"https://presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/reunion_devaluation_du_programme_de_developpement_a_la_base_des_145_territoires_presidee_ce_jour_par_le_chef_de_letat","claim":"Tshisekedi chaired an evaluation meeting on the 145 territories development program with the prime minister, sector ministers, and partner agencies, and the presidency said the identified projects were ready and the program comprised nearly 200 works such as hospitals and administrative buildings.","locator":"lines 71-74","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official account gives a concrete implementation milestone, though it is still government self-report.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Mid-2022 implementation inside the target year.","ruler_attribution":"High attribution: the meeting was chaired by Tshisekedi and tied to his named program.","contrary_evidence":["Readiness claims are official and not independently audited here."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.6","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"9eme conférence des gouverneurs: le président Tshisekedi se félicite de la stabilité des institutions provinciales et fait la promotion du pdl 145 T","publisher":"Presidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-12-22","url":"https://www.presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/9eme_conference_des_gouverneurs_le_president_tshisekedi_se_felicite_de_la_stabilite_des_institutions_provinciales_et_fait_la_promotion_du_pdl_145_t","claim":"Tshisekedi said provincial institutions had remained stable in 2022 and described PDL-145T as a program to promote territorial economies and improve rural living conditions through massive public investment.","locator":"lines 74-77","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official presidential report of a speech with explicit program framing and implementation intent.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Late-2022 period evidence, directly within target year.","ruler_attribution":"High attribution: the statement is directly Tshisekedi's and refers to his own program.","contrary_evidence":["Speech evidence does not confirm delivery or durability on its own."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.6","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Compte rendu de la cinquante-sixieme reunion du conseil des ministres","publisher":"Presidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-06-03","url":"https://www.presidence.cd/conseil-de-ministres/compte_rendu_de_la_cinquante_sixieme_reunion_du_conseil_des_ministres","claim":"Tshisekedi ordered strict enforcement of subcontracting rules through ARSP and, in the same meeting, directed ministries to fund and launch additional PDL-145 electrification and investment projects.","locator":"lines 89-99","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official minutes show concrete instructions and follow-up mechanisms, though implementation is not independently verified here.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"June 2022 inside the target year.","ruler_attribution":"High attribution: the instructions are explicitly attributed to Tshisekedi in a cabinet meeting he chaired.","contrary_evidence":["Minutes record instructions, not completion of the projects or sanctions."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.5","8B.6","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Compte rendu de la cinquante-sixieme reunion du conseil des ministres","publisher":"Presidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-06-03","url":"https://www.presidence.cd/conseil-de-ministres/compte_rendu_de_la_cinquante_sixieme_reunion_du_conseil_des_ministres","claim":"The same council meeting says the president credited a completed electrification project at Ipamu to his request and ordered budgetary ministries to pay for other investment projects in the ANSER pipeline.","locator":"lines 91-94","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official minutes provide a concrete implementation and resource-allocation directive.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"June 2022.","ruler_attribution":"High attribution: the action is described as undertaken at the president's request and under his instruction.","contrary_evidence":["A single showcased project may not reflect system-wide execution."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.8","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Discours du President de la Republique, Felix Tshisekedi sur l'etat de la nation","publisher":"Presidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-12-10","url":"https://www.presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/discours_du_president_de_la_republique_felix_tshisekedi_sur_letat_de_la_nation","claim":"In his end-of-year address, Tshisekedi said the government had worked across peace and security, state authority, education, anti-corruption, women's empowerment, universal health coverage, youth entrepreneurship, revenue mobilization, election preparation, and public-administration modernization.","locator":"lines 74-74","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official speech text lists the year's priority areas and claimed efforts.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"End of 2022, directly inside target year.","ruler_attribution":"High attribution: this is the ruler's own annual account of his government's program and execution.","contrary_evidence":["A speech is self-assessment and should be triangulated with independent outcome data."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.2","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Adresse a la nation du President de la Republique, Felix Tshisekedi suite a la deterioration de la situation securitaire a l'est du pays","publisher":"Presidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-11-03","url":"https://presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/adresse_a_la_nation_du_president_de_la_republique_felix_tshisekedi_suite_a_la_deterioration_de_la_situation_securitaire_a_lest_du_pays","claim":"Tshisekedi said the M23 advance had created a humanitarian crisis with more than 200,000 displaced people and that the government had been instructed to gather and care for them.","locator":"line 78","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct presidential address states the crisis scale and the government's response order.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"November 2022 within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"High attribution: the instruction is explicitly issued by the president during a live crisis.","contrary_evidence":["The underlying displacement is a negative external shock, not proof of competence by itself."],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Communique de Presse","publisher":"Presidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-07-06","url":"https://www.presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/communique_de_presse","claim":"After the Luanda summit, Tshisekedi backed a ceasefire, a de-escalation roadmap, the relaunch of the DRC-Rwanda joint commission, and the return of refugees as part of restoring trust and ending hostilities.","locator":"lines 73-79","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official communiqué records a concrete diplomatic mechanism and agreed steps.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"July 2022 target-year crisis management.","ruler_attribution":"High attribution: the communiqué reports Tshisekedi's direct participation and endorsement.","contrary_evidence":["The summit outcome depended on external mediation and the other party's compliance."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.6","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of the Congo: Staff Report for the 2022 Article IV Consultation, Second Review Under the Extended Credit Facility Arrangement","publisher":"International Monetary Fund","publication_date":"2022-07-05","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/publications/cr/issues/2022/07/05/democratic-republic-of-the-congo-staff-report-for-the-2022-article-iv-consultation-second-520400","claim":"The IMF said the DRC's macroeconomic environment had improved, the authorities had adopted prudent macroeconomic policies by halting central bank financing to the government, and further monetary, exchange-rate, natural-resource, and business-climate reforms were needed.","locator":"summary lines 269-271","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"IMF staff report is a strong independent macroeconomic source with explicit policy assessment.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Mid-2022 assessment of the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate-to-high attribution: these policies are attributed to the authorities under Tshisekedi, but some constraints are inherited and technocratic.","contrary_evidence":["IMF also says more reform is needed, so the record is mixed rather than definitive."],"lenses":["8B.3","8B.6","8B.7","8B.8","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of Congo Economic Update: Harnessing Growth Through Digital Connectivity to Create Jobs and Reduce Poverty","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-10-07","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/10/07/democratic-republic-of-congo-economic-update","claim":"The World Bank said growth rebounded strongly to 6.2 percent in 2021, but poverty reduction remained elusive; it also said the new telecom law and secondary legislation, fiber backbone investment, PPPs, and tax simplification were priority steps for digital-led growth and job creation.","locator":"lines 139-147","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"World Bank press release combines outcome assessment with concrete policy recommendations.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Late-2022 review of 2022 policy trajectory.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate-to-high attribution: macro growth is partly commodity-driven and not fully ruler-owned, but the reform agenda is government-directed.","contrary_evidence":["The report says poverty reduction was still elusive and much growth came from mining and external conditions."],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.7","8B.8","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"DR Congo: State Mining Company Subject to a Damning Audit","publisher":"OCCRP","publication_date":"2022-06-16","url":"https://www.occrp.org/en/news/dr-congo-state-mining-company-subject-to-a-damning-audit","claim":"The IGF audit of state mining company Gecamines was commissioned by President Tshisekedi and found severe irregularities, including embezzlement and the disappearance of $414 million that should have reached the central bank.","locator":"lines 42-48","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent investigative report citing the IGF audit and the president's commissioning of it.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Audit was commissioned before and finalized during 2022.","ruler_attribution":"High attribution for the commissioning decision; the underlying irregularities are company-level but within a state asset under presidential oversight.","contrary_evidence":["The audit concerns a state company with legacy problems and does not prove personal wrongdoing by Tshisekedi."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.5","8B.6","8B.8","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"The Democratic Republic of the Congo has achieved a high overall score in implementing the 2019 EITI Standard","publisher":"EITI","publication_date":"2022-10-13","url":"https://eiti.org/board-decision/2022-50","claim":"The EITI Board said DRC implementation generated tangible reforms with impetus from the Presidency, but also found beneficial-ownership rules only partly implemented and expressed concern about prosecutions of whistle-blowers.","locator":"lines 88-99 and 111-115","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"EITI validation is an authoritative external assessment combining performance and remaining gaps.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 validation outcome within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"High attribution for presidency-driven follow-through; partial implementation limits the strength of the positive inference.","contrary_evidence":["Beneficial ownership remained incomplete and whistleblower prosecutions cut against clean implementation."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.5","8B.6","8B.8","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"DR Congo: No Inquiry into Police Role in Ethnic Killings","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-05-23","url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/05/23/dr-congo-no-inquiry-police-role-ethnic-killings","claim":"Human Rights Watch said Congolese authorities took no disciplinary action and did not investigate police involvement in the Buhene attacks, and that Tshisekedi later appointed the police commander in charge at the time as deputy territory administrator.","locator":"lines 651-654","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent rights report provides a specific accountability failure and a ruler-linked appointment.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"May 2022 within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"High attribution for the appointment decision; the lack of inquiry reflects authority exercised under Tshisekedi.","contrary_evidence":["The article concerns a localized security episode, not the whole governing program."],"lenses":["8B.5","8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Top Congo presidential adviser resigns after allegedly requesting bribe on tape","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-09-16","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/top-congo-presidential-adviser-resigns-after-allegedly-requesting-bribe-on-tape-2894087","claim":"A top adviser to Tshisekedi resigned after a hidden-camera corruption allegation over a mineral deal; the report said the adviser claimed he could use his connections to Tshisekedi to bypass regulations in exchange for a cut.","locator":"lines 418-424","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting is strong on the resignation and the alleged taped conduct, though the underlying bribery allegation is not adjudicated here.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"September 2022 inside the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate attribution: the misconduct is by a close presidential adviser, not Tshisekedi personally, but it implicates his governing network and access control.","contrary_evidence":["The adviser denied wrongdoing, so the tape reveals allegations rather than a final finding."],"lenses":["8B.4","8B.5","8B.8","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Des proches de Tshisekedi accusés de corruption","publisher":"DW","publication_date":"2022-09-22","url":"https://www.dw.com/fr/rdc-corruption-vital-kamerhe-eteni-longondo-vidiye-tshimanga-f%C3%A9lix-tshisekedi/a-63211185","claim":"DW reported that several close associates of Tshisekedi were accused of corruption, that Tshisekedi had not yet reacted, and that Vidiye Tshimanga resigned after a video showed him negotiating a commission on a mining contract with fake investors.","locator":"lines 44-60","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent reporting captures the network-level scandal and the president's lack of immediate response.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"September 2022 within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate attribution: the conduct is network-level, and the article specifically notes the president had not reacted at publication time.","contrary_evidence":["The story centers on associates, so it is weaker for direct personal attribution than for network-control inference."],"lenses":["8B.4","8B.5","8B.8","8B.10"]}

**Ledger**
- Candidates found: about 30 plausible documents across official, IGO, NGO, and media families.
- Documents opened: 18 accessible documents and PDFs.
- Duplicate families removed: 10.
- Irrelevant or out-of-period items: 3.
- Inaccessible items: 2.
- Accepted distinct URLs in this wave: 17 new URLs, plus reused URLs from earlier batches relevant to 8B.
- Domain coverage in the dossier: 10 domains when reused evidence is included.

**Gaps**
- Direct 2022 evidence on budget execution, audited delivery, and actual completion rates for PDL-145T, ANSER electrification, and social-service spending is still thin.
- I did not find a clean 2022 primary record on presidential asset declarations, campaign finance, or personal/family business interests.
- The strongest remaining next queries are `Cour des comptes`, `IGF`, `BCECO`, `ANSER`, detailed 2022 budget execution reports, procurement and contract registries, and any 2022-2023 independent implementation audits for the 145 territories program and telecom reforms.
